---
title: 'Server-Side Rendering'
description: 'Render AG Charts to PNG and JPEG image buffers in Node.js without a browser.'
enterprise: true
---

The `ag-charts-server-side` package renders AG Charts to PNG and JPEG image buffers in Node.js, without a browser or DOM. Use it to generate chart images for email reports, PDF documents, social media cards, thumbnails, or API endpoints.

## Prerequisites

{% note %}
Server-side rendering requires Node.js 20.0.0 or later, and an [AG Charts Enterprise licence](./license-install/).
{% /note %}

## Installation

Install `ag-charts-server-side` alongside `ag-charts-community`:

{% tabs omitFromOverview=true snippetTabs=true %}
{% tabItem id="ssr-npm" label="NPM" %}

```bash
npm install ag-charts-server-side ag-charts-community
```

{% /tabItem %}
{% tabItem id="ssr-yarn" label="Yarn" %}

```bash
yarn add ag-charts-server-side ag-charts-community
```

{% /tabItem %}
{% /tabs %}

## Module Registration

Register modules before rendering any charts. This is typically done once at application startup:

```ts
import { AllCommunityModule, ModuleRegistry } from 'ag-charts-community';

ModuleRegistry.registerModules([AllCommunityModule]);
```

## Rendering a Chart

Call `AgChartsServerSide.render()` with chart options and output dimensions. The method returns a `Promise<Buffer>` containing the image data.

```ts
import * as fs from 'fs';
import { AllCommunityModule, ModuleRegistry } from 'ag-charts-community';
import { AgChartsServerSide } from 'ag-charts-server-side';

ModuleRegistry.registerModules([AllCommunityModule]);

const buffer = await AgChartsServerSide.render({
    options: {
        data: [
            { category: 'Q1', value: 10 },
            { category: 'Q2', value: 25 },
            { category: 'Q3', value: 15 },
            { category: 'Q4', value: 30 },
        ],
        series: [{ type: 'bar', xKey: 'category', yKey: 'value' }],
    },
    width: 400,
    height: 300,
});

fs.writeFileSync('chart.png', buffer);
```

{% imageCaption imagePath="resources/bar-chart-output.png" alt="Server-side rendered bar chart" constrained=true centered=true /%}

The `options` property accepts the same chart options as `AgCharts.create()`, excluding `container`, `width`, and `height` which are provided as top-level render options instead.

## Render Options

All render methods accept the following base options:

| Property     | Type              | Default | Description                                                  |
| ------------ | ----------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `width`      | `number`          | —       | Output image width in pixels.                                |
| `height`     | `number`          | —       | Output image height in pixels.                               |
| `format`     | `'png' \| 'jpeg'` | `'png'` | Output image format.                                         |
| `pixelRatio` | `number`          | `1`     | Pixel density multiplier for high-DPI output.                |
| `quality`    | `number`          | —       | JPEG quality 0–100 (only applies when `format` is `'jpeg'`). |
| `timeout`    | `number`          | `30000` | Render timeout in milliseconds.                              |

## JPEG Output

Set `format: 'jpeg'` to render JPEG images. Use `quality` to control the compression level.

```ts
const buffer = await AgChartsServerSide.render({
    options: {
        data: [{ x: 1, y: 2 }],
        series: [{ type: 'line', xKey: 'x', yKey: 'y' }],
    },
    width: 800,
    height: 600,
    format: 'jpeg',
    quality: 85,
});
```

## High-DPI Output

Set `pixelRatio` to produce higher-resolution images. The actual pixel dimensions of the output are `width * pixelRatio` by `height * pixelRatio`.

```ts
const buffer = await AgChartsServerSide.render({
    options: {
        data: [
            { x: 0, y: 0 },
            { x: 1, y: 5 },
            { x: 2, y: 3 },
        ],
        series: [{ type: 'line', xKey: 'x', yKey: 'y' }],
    },
    width: 200,
    height: 150,
    pixelRatio: 2,
});
// Output image is 400x300 actual pixels
```

## Enterprise Features

To use enterprise chart types such as waterfall, heatmap, or gauges, install the `ag-charts-enterprise` package and register `AllEnterpriseModule`:

{% tabs omitFromOverview=true snippetTabs=true %}
{% tabItem id="ent-npm" label="NPM" %}

```bash
npm install ag-charts-enterprise
```

{% /tabItem %}
{% tabItem id="ent-yarn" label="Yarn" %}

```bash
yarn add ag-charts-enterprise
```

{% /tabItem %}
{% /tabs %}

```ts
import { AllEnterpriseModule, LicenseManager, ModuleRegistry } from 'ag-charts-enterprise';

LicenseManager.setLicenseKey('your-licence-key');
ModuleRegistry.registerModules([AllEnterpriseModule]);
```

See [Enterprise Licence Key](./license-install/) for details on obtaining and configuring a licence key.

## Rendering Gauges

Use `AgChartsServerSide.renderGauge()` to render gauge charts. Pass gauge-specific options via the `options` property.

```ts
const buffer = await AgChartsServerSide.renderGauge({
    options: {
        type: 'radial-gauge',
        value: 75,
        scale: { min: 0, max: 100 },
    },
    width: 300,
    height: 300,
});
```

## Rendering Financial Charts

Use `AgChartsServerSide.renderFinancialChart()` to render financial charts with candlestick or OHLC series.

```ts
const buffer = await AgChartsServerSide.renderFinancialChart({
    options: {
        data: [
            { date: new Date('2024-01-02'), open: 100, high: 105, low: 98, close: 103 },
            { date: new Date('2024-01-03'), open: 103, high: 107, low: 101, close: 106 },
            { date: new Date('2024-01-04'), open: 106, high: 110, low: 104, close: 108 },
        ],
    },
    width: 800,
    height: 400,
});
```

## Custom Fonts

Use `AgChartsServerSide.loadFonts()` to register custom fonts before rendering. Each font definition specifies a family name, file path, and optional weight and style.

```ts
AgChartsServerSide.loadFonts([
    { family: 'CustomFont', path: '/path/to/CustomFont-Regular.ttf' },
    { family: 'CustomFont', path: '/path/to/CustomFont-Bold.ttf', weight: 'bold' },
    { family: 'CustomFont', path: '/path/to/CustomFont-Italic.ttf', style: 'italic' },
]);
```

## Concurrent Rendering

Multiple render calls can safely be issued concurrently. The package serialises rendering internally to prevent global state conflicts.

```ts
const charts = [
    { data: [{ x: 1, y: 10 }], width: 400, height: 300 },
    { data: [{ x: 1, y: 20 }], width: 400, height: 300 },
    { data: [{ x: 1, y: 30 }], width: 400, height: 300 },
];

const buffers = await Promise.all(
    charts.map((chart) =>
        AgChartsServerSide.render({
            options: {
                data: chart.data,
                series: [{ type: 'line', xKey: 'x', yKey: 'y' }],
            },
            width: chart.width,
            height: chart.height,
        })
    )
);
```

## Express.js Integration

Serve chart images from an HTTP endpoint:

```ts
import express from 'express';
import { AllCommunityModule, ModuleRegistry } from 'ag-charts-community';
import { AgChartsServerSide } from 'ag-charts-server-side';

ModuleRegistry.registerModules([AllCommunityModule]);

const app = express();

app.get('/chart.png', async (req, res) => {
    const buffer = await AgChartsServerSide.render({
        options: {
            data: [
                { category: 'Q1', value: 10 },
                { category: 'Q2', value: 25 },
                { category: 'Q3', value: 15 },
                { category: 'Q4', value: 30 },
            ],
            series: [{ type: 'bar', xKey: 'category', yKey: 'value' }],
        },
        width: 800,
        height: 600,
    });

    res.set('Content-Type', 'image/png');
    res.send(buffer);
});

app.listen(3000);
```

## API Reference

### AgChartsServerSide

| Method                          | Returns           | Description                                   |
| ------------------------------- | ----------------- | --------------------------------------------- |
| `render(options)`               | `Promise<Buffer>` | Renders a standard chart to an image buffer.  |
| `renderGauge(options)`          | `Promise<Buffer>` | Renders a gauge chart to an image buffer.     |
| `renderFinancialChart(options)` | `Promise<Buffer>` | Renders a financial chart to an image buffer. |
| `loadFonts(fonts)`              | `void`            | Registers custom fonts for rendering.         |

### BaseRenderOptions

All render methods accept these base options alongside a chart-type-specific `options` property.

| Property     | Type              | Required | Description                                          |
| ------------ | ----------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |
| `width`      | `number`          | Yes      | Output image width in pixels.                        |
| `height`     | `number`          | Yes      | Output image height in pixels.                       |
| `format`     | `'png' \| 'jpeg'` | No       | Output image format. Default: `'png'`.               |
| `pixelRatio` | `number`          | No       | Pixel density multiplier. Default: `1`.              |
| `quality`    | `number`          | No       | JPEG quality 0–100 (only when `format` is `'jpeg'`). |
| `timeout`    | `number`          | No       | Render timeout in milliseconds. Default: `30000`.    |

### Chart Options by Render Method

Each render method extends `BaseRenderOptions` with a chart-type-specific `options` property. The `container`, `width`, and `height` properties are excluded from `options` as they are provided as top-level render options.

| Method                   | `options` Type            |
| ------------------------ | ------------------------- |
| `render()`               | `AgChartOptions`          |
| `renderGauge()`          | `AgGaugeOptions`          |
| `renderFinancialChart()` | `AgFinancialChartOptions` |

### FontDefinition

| Property | Type     | Required | Description                                        |
| -------- | -------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------- |
| `family` | `string` | Yes      | Font family name used in chart options.            |
| `path`   | `string` | Yes      | File path to the font file (`.ttf`, `.otf`, etc.). |
| `weight` | `string` | No       | Font weight (e.g., `'bold'`, `'600'`).             |
| `style`  | `string` | No       | Font style (e.g., `'italic'`).                     |
